    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal">
        <tei:div facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg">
          <tei:pb ed="1965" n="3" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg"/>
          <tei:note type="description" xml:lang="en">The Thirteen Principles</tei:note>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/1" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/1"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>Exalted is the living God and praised. He exists and timeless is His existence. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/2" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/2"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He is unique and there is nought unique like His uniqueness. He is hidden and infinite too is His unity. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/3" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/3"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He has not the shape of a body nor is He a body. We cannot estimate His sanctity. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/4" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/4"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He was there before anything that was created; He is the first and there was no beginning to His beginning. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/5" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/5"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>Behold He is the Master of the world and every creature indicates His grandeur and His rule. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/6" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/6"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>The wealth of His prophecy did He bestow upon men of His possession and His glory. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/7" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/7"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>No other prophet arose in Israel like Moses, who perceived His likeness. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/8" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/8"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>The true Torah has God given to His people through His prophet, the faithful one of His house. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/9" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/9"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>God will not alter nor will He change His law for another unto eternity. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/10" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/10"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He observes and knows our secrets, perceiving even at its beginning the end of a matter. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/11" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/11"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He treats man kindly according to his conduct and sends disaster to the wicked according to his wickedness. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/12" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/12"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>He will send our Messiah at the end of days to redeem those who wait for the finality of His salvation. </tei:p>
          <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="stanza" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/day_two/morning_occurrences/yigdal/quote/poem/yigdal_daniel/13" source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:poem:yigdal_daniel/13"/><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-sheni-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-two-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n28.jpg" n="3"/>God <tei:choice><tei:sic>wiil</tei:sic><tei:corr>will</tei:corr></tei:choice> revive the dead in the abundance of His grace. Blessed for ever and ever be His renowned Name. <tei:milestone unit="stanza"/></tei:p>
        </tei:div>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
